# 40 — Discover and reuse others' packs and contributions

**Project:** Discover and reuse others' packs and contributions

**Goal:** Give creators and agents a streamlined way to discover other contributors' packs, components and creative work, with Hivemind-backed search, provenance, compatibility and maintenance signals.

**Status:** queued

**Owner:** Unassigned

**Estimate:** TBD

**Waiting on:** owner/scope agreement; source and dependency checks

**Start:** [Astrid development skill](../../skills/astrid-dev/SKILL.md) and [shared run contract](../../skills/astrid-dev-shared/run-contract.md). [Inputs](inputs.md) · [Tasks](tasks.md). The [catalog](../index.md) owns priority, status and owner.

**Vision gaps:** [CA-004 — Discover and reuse others' packs and contributions](../../vision/gaps/CA-004-sharing-and-discovery.md) (primary).

## Goal and scope

Give creators and agents a streamlined way to discover other contributors' packs, components and creative work, with Hivemind-backed search, provenance, compatibility and maintenance signals.

**Included:** Publish a minimal searchable contribution index for people and agents; include identity, licenses, compatibility, ownership, versions, and removal. Search may use Hivemind knowledge but should not depend on unproven federation.

**Boundary:** Do not own pack installation, automatic execution or external-web ingestion; those belong to Plan 06 and Plan 42.

## What this builds on

Existing pack metadata and contribution flows plus [Plan 22's Hivemind](../22-hivemind-protocol/plan.md). These are foundations to verify at current source revisions, not proof of a deployed result. Prefer reusing them over inventing another runtime or state owner.

## Proposed sequence

1. Inspect existing pack metadata, community contribution routes and Hivemind search.
2. Define publication, revision/removal, ownership and trust metadata in the existing contracts.
3. Offer human and agent task-aware discovery of published work, with transparent source and compatibility.
4. Test an unrelated author publishing and a separate creator and agent finding and reusing a contribution; include untrusted, outdated and unavailable cases.

## Interfaces and handoff

Before product work, pin actual accepted base/donor revisions, implementation owners and dependencies. Consume existing pack/component/project contracts; produce a tested contract or working artifact and link exact product PRs. Never infer authorization from a draft.

## Completion

Test an unrelated author publishing and a separate creator and agent finding and reusing a contribution; include untrusted, outdated and unavailable cases. Record integrated candidate identity, real creator/agent outcomes and meaningful negative cases. Completion does not automatically close the associated vision gap.

**Authorization:** Draft, unassigned, queued. Owner decision and focused checks are required before implementation.
